<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Synod of Dort</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1618">1618</a>–<a href="/years/1619">1619</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Synod of Dordrecht</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Synod of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dordrecht">Dort</a> was an international assembly of the Reformed churches held at Dordrecht in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in 1618–1619. Called to settle the dispute between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/remonstrants">Arminians</a> (Remonstrants) and strict Calvinists, it rejected the Arminian position, adopted the Canons of Dort on predestination and grace, and approved the Belgic Confession and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg-catechism">Heidelberg Catechism</a>. Its decisions became standards of Reformed orthodoxy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/synod-of-dort.jpg" alt="Synod of Dort" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pouwels Weyts de Jonge (Dordrecht, 01-01-1585 - Delft, 26-05-1629) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Synode_van_Dordrecht.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
